/E (The reduction in petrol loading costs by Dangote Refinery reflects the ongoing fluctuations in global crude oil markets. Brent crude, the international benchmark, was traded at $77.48 per barrel on January 31, 2025, marking a reduction from $81 per barrel recorded in early January. This move aligns with the refinery's commitment to transparency and fairness, aiming to pass on the benefits of lower crude prices to consumers.)
